/-
L4Factoidal.HTML.Entities — character references of the WHATWG HTML Living
Standard, §13.2.5.72 to §13.2.5.80 ("Character reference state" and the
states it calls), and the table of §13.5 ("Named character references").

Implemented: every numeric reference, with the replacement rules of the
"Numeric character reference end state" (NUL, out of range, surrogate,
noncharacter, control, and the C1 table of windows-1252); the named references
that the Living Standard lists with a trailing semicolon and that fall in
these groups: ASCII markup (`amp lt gt quot apos`), the 96 Latin-1
names of HTML 4 (`nbsp` to `yuml`), Greek letters, general punctuation,
arrows, common mathematical operators and a few symbols. The 96 Latin-1 names
and `amp lt gt quot` (with the upper-case forms `AMP LT GT QUOT`) are also
the references that the standard allows without the closing semicolon.

The full table of names with a semicolon (2,125 names, multi-codepoint ones
included) is `HTML.EntityData` (generated by `tools/html/gen-entities.py`
from the WHATWG `entities.json`); `namedRef?` reads it. A name outside the
table is treated as an unknown named reference (error
`unknown-named-character-reference` and the text is kept).
-/
import Std.Data.HashMap
import L4Factoidal.HTML.EntityData

namespace L4Factoidal.HTML

